s, footwear, and home-fashioned products for the entire family. It sells its products to middle income households and households with lower to more moderate incomes. Ross Stores, Inc. was incorporated in 1957 and is headquartered in Dublin, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James G. Conroy | CEO & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $6.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 111K people. Revenue per employee of $205K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 33\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Ross Stores, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $74.1B market cap on $22.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 80% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 71-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $2.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.41\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 49\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 40% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3973735058433687},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $17.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ross Stores (NASDAQ:ROST) Stock 